{# This round's stimulus in the SHARDED cell of the subagent-kill design
   (spec §6.2): the disclosed shape, then a pointer to the subagents that
   hold this round's examples, then the query signal.

   INVARIANT: this file and observation_puzzle.j2 differ in the EXAMPLES
   block and nowhere else -- the ``ROUND N.`` header, the indented shape
   line, ``NOW:`` and ``ACTIONS:`` are the same text in the same order, so
   the sharded and control cells differ in where the examples live and in
   nothing else. (Spec 6.2 also showed a closing "Write this round's rule
   in one line..." line here; that was an error in the spec -- the sentence
   is probe_puzzle.j2, which the turn renders as its own call, and
   observation_puzzle.j2 has never carried it.) Pinned by
   tests/unit/test_clue_sharding.py::test_the_two_cells_differ_only_in_the_examples_block.

   Supervisor voice (prompt revision v2): ``LABEL: sentence`` headers, no
   ``=== X ===`` marker, one or two CAPS words per sentence. The examples
   sentence never says how many examples there are, how they are spread
   over the slots, or how many of them matter -- a slot may hold several
   (capacity = ceil(|M| / required_slots)) and the count would hand the
   player the round's threshold.

   The shape stays on its own indented line in exactly the grammar the
   RULE field and ``parse_rule_text`` accept: filling every blank of that
   string is a well-formed answer.

   Variables:
     turn_number : int          -- this round's number
     shape_line : str           -- render_shape_hint(puzzle.shape)
     subagents_alive_str : str  -- comma-joined alive slot names
     query : str                -- this round's new signal
     actions_str : str          -- comma-joined action list
     main_clues : list[str]     -- OPTIONAL (team-wallet design, plan
         2026-09-17 sec. 4). When main_holds_bundle deals the main agent a
         pile, its clue texts go here and are listed inline above the
         pointer sentence, in observation_puzzle.j2's ``  - clue`` format
         and in the place that template puts its examples. The pointer
         sentence then says "The other bundles" instead of "This round's
         examples", because one of them is on the board. Empty / undefined
         renders byte-identically to every run before this existed --
         pinned by
         tests/unit/test_clue_sharding.py::TestFlagOffIsByteIdentical.
     consult : bool -- OPTIONAL (decision-first design, plan 2026-09-21
         T3). The consult protocol: the task call may spend one reply
         asking named subagents for their bundles instead of answering,
         and the ASKING block is where that option is stated. It is
         appended LAST, after ACTIONS:, because it is about how to
         reply and not about the round. The block names no count and no
         threshold, exactly as the pointer sentence above does not --
         "each subagent that is still with you" is the roster the
         status block already stated. Absent / false renders the bytes
         every run before this had, pinned by
         tests/unit/test_team_wallet_v2_prompts.py.

         It ALSO drops one sentence (2026-09-21, controller ruling in
         plan T4 fix 1): "Ask a subagent for its examples by calling it."
         is Agent-tool-era wording -- in that design a subagent WAS a
         tool and calling it was the mechanism. Under the consult
         protocol there is no tool and the mechanism is the ASK line
         below, which states itself; leaving both in told the agent to
         call something and then told it how to ask instead. Only that
         sentence goes, and only when the flag is on: the EXAMPLES line
         still says where the other bundles are, which is the fact the
         round turns on.
#}ROUND {{ turn_number }}.
THE RULE'S SHAPE (fill in the blanks):

    {{ shape_line }}

{% if main_clues %}EXAMPLES (yours): You hold the bundle below, all following this round's rule.
{% for clue in main_clues %}  - {{ clue }}
{% endfor %}{% endif %}EXAMPLES: {% if main_clues %}The other bundles are{% else %}This round's examples are{% endif %} held by your subagents. {% if not (consult is defined and consult) %}Ask a subagent for its examples by calling it. {% endif %}Subagents alive: {{ subagents_alive_str }}.
{% set query_list = queries if queries is defined else [query] %}{% if query_list | length > 1 %}{% for q in query_list %}NOW {{ loop.index }}: {{ q }}.
{% endfor %}{% else %}NOW: {{ query_list[0] }}.
{% endif %}ACTIONS: [{{ actions_str }}]
{% if consult is defined and consult %}ASKING: Each subagent that is still with you holds one bundle of this round's examples. To hear a subagent's bundle, reply with exactly one line: ASK: <subagent names separated by commas>. You will then be asked for your answer. Or answer now.
{% endif %}